+## §4.4
+
+- 2026-11-13 (TD-1557): A board line's slot answer is filled from the person's words. Paul typed a `Hold: <note>`
+  answer into a Queue card's Answer… on an end-of-rounds `decide` line on 2026-11-07, and it went as a Reply,
+  deciding nothing, since §4.4 *Decide* took only an offered answer or a filled `Not right: <what>`, while screen 12
+  and §4.5a said Answer… took the line's decided line; and the `Hold: <note>` button decided with the placeholder
+  as written. Settled: any form `<label>: <slot>` is filled as the look's was, by ledgerboard's `slot_label` and
+  `fill_slot` (TD-9001); words of any other shape are a Reply; a form is never taken as a default. Builds TD-9001, TD-9002.
+
+- 2026-11-13 (TD-1557's review, rounds 1–6, the wide cap; record `docs/reviews/TD-1557.md`): fact-checks R1, R4, R7,
+  R10, R13, R16 and the closing R19 (0 build-changing, 5 minor) with its re-runs R20 (2 minor) and R21 (nothing); Fable
+  R2, R5, R8, R11, R14, R17; Sonnet R3, R6, R9, R12, R15, R18 — 111 findings, build-changing per round in the design
+  reviews 10, 4, 1, 1, 3, 1, the fact-checks' 1, 1, 0, 0, 1, 0. A form is never taken as a default, and the writer
+  is unchanged, since cadence §4.8 lets an end-of-rounds item recommend `Hold: <note>` (F35); the page reads Answer…
+  by four comparisons against the server's lists, `fill_slot` the one filler (F9, F19, F30, F46, F60); kept words
+  carry the road of the box they were typed in (F66, F82, F95); a changed `Answers:` meets its key's refusal first
+  (F81); the box binds whether the line is open and undecided (F101, unread by a review, so the end-of-rounds item
+  recommends One more round).
+
+## §4.5
+
+- 2026-11-13 (TD-1557): Answer… on a Queue card's board item is the line's decide when its words, whitespace
+  collapsed, are one of its answers word for word or fill one of its forms, and a Reply otherwise, the box saying
+  which as the words are typed; a form is drawn as its label with an ellipsis (**Hold…**) and opens its row's box
+  with the label begun. Chosen over keeping Answer… a Reply always, which would leave the card no way to fill a
+  `Hold: <note>` but its own button.
+
+## §4.5a
+
+- 2026-11-13 (TD-1557): Row *Due strip / Inbox board row: a slot answer* added (**<label>…**); the board answers
+  row, the pending mark and *Queue card: answers, Answer…* say what Answer… and a form send on a board line.
+
+## §4.10
+
+- 2026-11-13 (TD-1557): A form is never taken as a default: the home refuses a steer's default that is a form, a pick
+  of one, and a reply that is one with no words; a form may still be an ask's recommended answer.
