+## TD-9001: Bump the agent-cadence pin to the release whose ledgerboard fills a slot answer such as Hold: <note>
+
+**Priority:** Medium
+**Type:** feature
+**Added:** 2026-11-13
+**Owner:** grinder
+**Kind:** build
+**Status:** Open
+**Blocked by:** decision (paul), event (agent-cadence-slot)
+**Part of:** TD-1557
+**Location:** docs/cadence.toml; src/sessionorc/ledgerboard/
+
+**Why:** TD-1557's design fills a slot answer, `<label>: <slot>` such as an end-of-rounds item's `Hold: <note>`, from the person's words (design §4.4 *Decide*). The form's reading is ledgerboard's, the board format's one parser (§8 *No second parser*), which today knows only the look's `Not right: <what>` (`is_not_right_form`, `fill_not_right` in `src/sessionorc/ledgerboard/__init__.py`). The generalised reading is a ledgerboard release, asked of ledgerboard's question seat (`ao td add --repo ledgerboard`) by TD-1557's designer when its rounds end, who in the same act asks agent-cadence's seat (`ao td add --repo agent-cadence`) to vendor the ledgerboard release that carries it, blocked there on the first, TD-1557's Status naming both asks, and vendored by agent-cadence; this build brings it here, so TD-9002 can call it.
+
+**Ask:** Held with its design TD-1557 until Paul answers its end-of-rounds item (One more round, Go or Hold) on docs/user_attention.md.
+
+**Event (agent-cadence-slot):** agent-cadence's vendored ledgerboard fills a slot answer.
+check: file-contains agent-cadence files/scripts/ledgerboard/__init__.py "def fill_slot"
+
+**Fix:** What ledgerboard's release carries (the ask names it, and this build checks it is there):
+- `slot_label(answer) -> str | None`: the label of an answer that is a form, whitespace collapsed — a label, not empty, holding no `:`, `<`, `>` or `|`, then a colon, any space and one `<…>` placeholder, empty or holding no `<`, `>`, `:` or `/`, ending the answer (`Hold: <note>` gives `Hold`; `Not right:<what>` and `Hold: <>` are forms; `See: <https://x>` is not), or `Not right:` alone (`Not right`) — and for the label `Not right` any placeholder `NOT_RIGHT_FORM_RE` takes (`<a/b>` too), so every look pair's form is a form — else None; the label is returned trimmed. It reads a label as `parse_answers` gives it, mark and consequence removed.
+- `fill_slot(said, offered) -> str | None`: `offered` the item's labels as `parse_answers` gives them; with `said` whitespace collapsed, None when `said` holds no colon (`Hold` alone names no form) or its part before its first colon, trimmed, is no form's label among `offered`, ignoring case by `str.lower()` on both (`Hold : keep` matches `Hold`); where it is, the first such form's label as offered, a colon, a space and the words after the colon, so `hold: keep Dismiss` fills `Hold: <note>` as `Hold: keep Dismiss`; `Refused` when nothing, or a lone `<…>` placeholder (any `<…>` with no `<` or `>` inside, so `Hold: <https://x>` too), follows the colon — *<label> needs its words*, or *Not right needs its words: say what is off* where the label as offered is `Not right`, on any line (the page's own line under the box is always the generic *<label> needs its words*). An offered answer word for word is the caller's to try first.
+- `is_not_right_form` kept as it is (`NOT_RIGHT_FORM_RE`), for the look's pair (`inbox.live_look`, `look_pair`), so no look stops being a pair; `fill_not_right`, whose one caller here (`_board_answer`) TD-9002 moves to `fill_slot`, may go once no consumer names it.
+- No writer change: a form may be marked ` (default)` as the recommended answer (cadence §4.8's end-of-rounds item may recommend `Hold: <note>`); that nothing takes it with no words is the consumers' (TD-9002).
+
+This build: once agent-cadence's vendored ledgerboard carries `fill_slot` (its **Event (agent-cadence-slot)** section), bump this repo's pin to that agent-cadence commit with `agent-cadence bump`, in a reviewed PR, and bring the vendored copy with it: `scripts/vendor_ledgerboard.sh` at the new tag, `tests/ledgerboard.vendored` rewritten and the `tests/ledgerboard/` fixtures refreshed (`tests/test_ledgerboard_fixtures.py` holds them). Check that `slot_label` and `fill_slot` are there and read as above; if the release lacks any, say so on TD-9002 and ask ledgerboard's seat again with `ao td add --repo ledgerboard`.
+
+**Done when:** This repo's `docs/cadence.toml` pins an agent-cadence commit whose `scripts/ledgerboard/__init__.py` has `slot_label` and `fill_slot` as above, `src/sessionorc/ledgerboard/` matches it, and in this repo `ledgerboard.fill_slot("hold : keep Dismiss", ["Go", "Hold: <note>"])` gives `Hold: keep Dismiss` while `fill_slot("Hold: <b>", …)` and `fill_slot("Hold:", …)` are refused and `fill_slot("Hold", …)` gives None; and `slot_label` gives `Hold` for `Hold: <>`, `Not right` for `Not right:<what>` and for `Not right:` alone, and None for `See: <https://x>` and `: <x>`.
+
+**Log:**
+- 2026-11-13: gate added: decision (paul)
