+**Why:** TD-1557's design (§4.4 *Decide*, §4.5 screen 12 *Three verbs*, §4.5a row *Due strip / Inbox board row: a slot answer*) settles what a board `decide` line's **Answer…** writes and how a slot answer is filled. Today the agent's `_board_answer` (`src/sessionorc/agent_inbox.py`) accepts an offered answer word for word, so an end-of-rounds item's `Hold: <note>` button decides with the placeholder as written, and a Queue card's Answer… on a board item always takes the Reply road (`board_answer`, `data-act="board_reply"` in `src/shiftlead/ui/templates/inbox_row.html`), so Paul's typed `Hold: …` on 2026-11-07 decided nothing (TD-1555, TD-1554).
