+# TD-1557: A board decide line's Answer… and its Hold: <note> answer
+
+## What it does
+
+- Some answers have a blank for your words, like an end-of-rounds item's Hold: <note> or a look's Not right: <what>.
+  They are now drawn as Hold… and open a box with "Hold:" already typed. Your words fill the blank and are written
+  as your decision, "Hold: keep Dismiss". Pressing the bare Hold: <note> can no longer be recorded as a decision.
+- Answer… on a Queue card's board item now answers the line when your words are one of its answers, or fill one
+  of its blanks. Any other words are written on the line as a reply, and the item keeps waiting for an answer.
+  While you type, the box says which it will do: "decides: …", that Hold still wants your words, or
+  "replies on the line".
+- On a look, a filled Not right through Answer… still hands an entry to the repo's techlead, as Not right… does.
+- Every road a press can take checks this the same way: the board, a ledger entry's decision, mail, and the
+  command line. A blank answer sent with no words is refused, with words saying what to send instead.
+
+## The key choices, and why
+
+- Answer… decides only when its words match an answer. Free words cannot say whether a held design is lifted or
+  kept waiting, so they stay a reply. The row's own Reply is always a reply.
+- A Hold note keeps the design held and reaches its designer as the answered line, as before, now with your note.
+- The way a blank is read is ledgerboard's, the shared board format, so every repo reads it the same way. That
+  part is asked of ledgerboard and agent-cadence when the rounds end, and the pin bump brings it here.
+- A blank answer may still be the recommended one, outlined, since the cadence lets a design recommend Hold. But
+  nothing takes it without words: no Go with it is drawn for it, and a steer cannot have one as its default.
+- Words a refused or closed box held are kept for the next box that would send them the same way, never for a
+  plain Reply, which would turn your decision into a note.
+
+## What it rules out
+
+- Typing any words into Answer… as a decision; only an offered answer or a filled blank decides.
+- Go with it taking a blank answer with no words, and a new steer having one as its default (a steer sent before
+  this still lapses as any does, its default being its sender's own plan).
+- A second reading of the format in the page: it compares your words against lists the server hands it, and the
+  server checks again before anything is written.
+
+## What you will see
+
+- Hold… on an end-of-rounds item, on the Inbox and on its Queue card, opening a box with "Hold:" begun.
+- Under Answer… on a board item, a line saying whether your words decide or reply, before you send.
+- If the line changed while you typed, a refusal that puts your words where you can copy them.
+- In ao inbox, a blank answer printed without a number, with "(reply Hold: your words)" beside it.
